SCALING CHECK (Test A vs Test B, sign=+1, ds=0.25):
==============================================================================
root ||F||_max ratio  (loose/tight) = 1.024e+08
PASS criterion: movement ratio should track (be of comparable
order to, not wildly exceed) the residual ratio -- movement
that is O(1) regardless of root quality would be the DAE-leakage
signature (constraint/mass-term touching non-evolution rows).
step |z_new-z_old|_max (tight) = 0.000e+00 -- below the 1e-13 noise floor (step() returned at k=0, no correction computed); a loose/tight RATIO is undefined here, not large. Falling back to an absolute bar on the loose-root movement instead:
  loose |z_new-z_old|_max = 8.628e-04  vs  bar = 5.337e-03
>>> loose-root movement is within the residual-scaled bar -- no leakage signature at this scale.

